# Normalize line endings for everything tracked here.
#
# The build/test/release pipeline runs on Linux (GitHub Actions runners and
# the containers built from this tree). Shell scripts, the Makefile, Docker
# files and systemd units break outright if they pick up CRLF: the kernel
# reads `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` as an interpreter path that does not exist,
# and `make` chokes on the trailing `\r` in every rule.
#
# This repo is also edited from Windows checkouts, where `core.autocrlf=true`
# is a common global default. Pinning `text=auto` here makes Git store LF in
# the repository regardless of the local setting, so a Windows edit can no
# longer silently rewrite a script. Keep this file in sync with the toolchain
# expectations of the release workflow.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xz   binary
*.gz   binary
*.tgz  binary
*.zip  binary
*.so   binary
*.onnx binary
